# Two same-named weak commons of different sizes (4 and 16 bytes, smaller
# one first) must resolve to the larger size, matching real common-merge
# semantics, rather than whichever occurrence the linker happened to see
# first. weak_common_3_anchor lands right after, so its address reflects
# how much storage weak_common_3 actually reserved.
0+ W weak_common_3
0+10 B weak_common_3_anchor
